    <string name="about_body_text">Muscle Tracker is a minimalistic workout tracker built for lifting. Create custom workouts, log sets as you train, and see your progress over time. With features including rest timers, weight suggestions, PR tracking, and one rep maximum estimates.\n\nEverything stays on your device. No accounts, no ads — just a straightforward way to record what you lift.\n\nBuilt by jpalayoor.</string>
    <string name="feedback_prompt_text">Questions or feedback? Feedback here:</string>
    <string name="email_text">muscletracker@jpalayoor.com</string>
    <string name="privacy_body_text">Muscle Tracker does not collect, transmit, retain or share any of your data.\n\nEverything you enter — templates, workout sessions, sets, weights, reps — is stored only in a local database on this device. Nothing is sent to a server, because this app doesn\'t have one.\n\nThere are no accounts, no analytics, no ads, and no third-party tracking of any kind.\n\nThe only way your data ever leaves this device is if you choose to use the Export feature in Settings, which lets you save a backup file yourself. That file goes wherever you choose to save it — it is never sent anywhere automatically.\n\nUninstalling the app permanently deletes everything, since nothing exists outside of it.</string>
    <string name="step1_title">1. Create a template</string>
    <string name="step1_body">Go to Workouts and tap + to name a new template, like "Push."</string>
    <string name="step2_title">2. Add exercises</string>
    <string name="step2_body">Tap into your template, then tap + to search and select the exercises you want in it.</string>
    <string name="step3_title">3. Start a workout</string>
    <string name="step3_body">From Home or Record, tap Start Workout and pick a template to begin a session.</string>
    <string name="step4_title">4. Log your sets</string>
    <string name="step4_body">Tap an exercise, enter your weight and reps, and tap Log Set. Your previous performance and a suggested weight show up automatically, and a rest timer starts after each set.</string>
    <string name="step5_title">5. Finish and move on</string>
    <string name="step5_body">Tap Finish Exercise to return to the list, and repeat for each exercise. When you\'re done, tap the checkmark in the header to end the workout.</string>
    <string name="step6_title">6. Review your history</string>
    <string name="step6_body">Your stats, personal records, and full workout history are always available on Home and Record.</string>
</resources>